@page "/Help"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Help"; }
<main data-page="help">
    <h1>Help</h1>
    <div class="card">
        <h3>Saving and opening</h3>
        <p>While you are connected, open <b>Resources</b> and press <b>Save</b>. The resource is stored on this device. Press <b>Open</b> at any time, with or without internet.</p>
        <h3>What the status means</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Available offline:</b> saved on this device. The date shows when your lease expires.</li>
            <li><b>Not stored on this device:</b> press Save while connected.</li>
            <li><b>Update available:</b> the University published a newer version. Press Update while connected.</li>
            <li><b>Lease expired: connect to renew:</b> the University limits how long a copy can be used. Connect to the internet and press Renew. You do not need to download the file again.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>If a resource will not open</h3>
        <p>The message tells you why: the lease expired, the stored file was changed, or the device date and time are wrong. Connect to the internet, press <b>Sync now</b>, then try again. If a file was changed, remove it and save it again.</p>
        <h3>Synchronising</h3>
        <p>When you are online the app synchronises automatically. It sends your task progress and a record of your offline use, and it applies any change the University made, such as a withdrawn or replaced resource.</p>
        <h3>Removing a resource</h3>
        <p>Press <b>Remove</b> to delete the copy from this device and free the space.</p>
    </div>
</main>
